//RS //! Semantic checks. Everything here exists so that codegen can stay "dumb"
//RS //! (invariant I3): by the time a Program reaches codegen, it must be
//RS //! impossible for the generated Rust to fail to compile (invariant I2).
//RS //!
//RS //! M1: type inference, mutability, definite-return analysis.
//RS //! M2: ownership — moves, call-site `&`/`^`,
//RS //! view returns, use-after-move, and borrow rules that keep generated Rust
//RS //! sound without surfacing Rust concepts to users.
